{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_12-31-30-hashicorp_raft-real-run/agent-source && grep -n 'func (r \\\\*Raft) configurationChangeChIfStable' -A 12 raft.go | head -16; grep -n 'func nextConfiguration' configuration.go; grep -n 'func (c \\\\*commitment) setConfiguration' -A 10 commitment.go | head -12; grep -n 'func (r \\\\*Raft) appendConfigurationEntry' -A 6 raft.go | head -8\"","aggregated_output":"654:func (r *Raft) configurationChangeChIfStable() chan *configurationChangeFuture {\n655-\t// Have to wait until:\n656-\t// 1. The latest configuration is committed, and\n657-\t// 2. This leader has committed some entry (the noop) in this term\n658-\t//    https://groups.google.com/forum/#!msg/raft-dev/t4xj6dJTP6E/d2D9LrWRza8J\n659-\tif r.configurations.latestIndex == r.configurations.committedIndex &&\n660-\t\tr.getCommitIndex() >= r.leaderState.commitment.startIndex {\n661-\t\treturn r.configurationChangeCh\n662-\t}\n663-\treturn nil\n664-}\n665-\n666-// leaderLoop is the hot loop for a leader. It is invoked\n224:func nextConfiguration(current Configuration, currentIndex uint64, change configurationChangeRequest) (Configuration, error) {\n53:func (c *commitment) setConfiguration(configuration Configuration) {\n54-\tc.Lock()\n55-\tdefer c.Unlock()\n56-\toldMatchIndexes := c.matchIndexes\n57-\tc.matchIndexes = make(map[ServerID]uint64)\n58-\tfor _, server := range configuration.Servers {\n59-\t\tif server.Suffrage == Voter {\n60-\t\t\tc.matchIndexes[server.ID] = oldMatchIndexes[server.ID] // defaults to 0\n61-\t\t}\n62-\t}\n63-\tc.recalculate()\n1204:func (r *Raft) appendConfigurationEntry(future *configurationChangeFuture) {\n1205-\tconfiguration, err := nextConfiguration(r.configurations.latest, r.configurations.latestIndex, future.req)\n1206-\tif err != nil {\n1207-\t\tfuture.respond(err)\n1208-\t\treturn\n1209-\t}\n1210-\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_12-31-30-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nsub = {\n \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Registered the one consequence channel the exercised account leaves untested, as a necessary gap with its source basis rather than a claim: membership changes are computed from the reconstructed configuration and committed under the commitment built from it, so a client AddVoter or RemoveServer issued on a node whose configuration is the reconstruction can rewrite the committed membership without the previous configuration's majority. Two source-grounded behaviours record the mechanism, the gap keeps it open, and the discriminator now names it.\\\",\n \\\"sources\\\": [\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"change_gate\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":654,\\\"end_line\\\":664,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"append_config_change\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1204,\\\"end_line\\\":1243,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"next_configuration\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"configuration.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":224,\\\"end_line\\\":240,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"commitment_set_config\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"commitment.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":53,\\\"end_line\\\":63,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}\n ],\n \\\"knowledge\\\": [\n  {\\\"ref\\\": \\\"@client_change_on_reconstructed_leader\\\",\n   \\\"kind\\\": \\\"behavior\\\",\n   \\\"statement\\\": \\\"A leader accepts a client membership change as soon as its own latest configuration is committed and it has committed an entry in its term (configurationChangeChIfStable), then computes the new configuration with nextConfiguration from configurations.latest and the request, appends it, immediately installs it as the latest configuration and rebuilds the leader's commitment from it; the request's prevIndex, when nonzero, is the only guard against acting on a different configuration than the caller expected.\\\",\n   \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"The node is leader and its configurations.latest is the one reconstructed at startup rather than the configuration recorded in its log; a client calls AddVoter, AddNonvoter, DemoteVoter or RemoveServer with prevIndex 0 (the package's AddPeer and RemovePeer helpers use 0, and callers may too); the gate does not consult the log's own configuration entry.\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"change_gate\\\",\\\"append_config_change\\\",\\\"next_configuration\\\",\\\"commitment_set_config\\\",\\\"leader_commitment\\\"]},\n  {\\\"ref\\\": \\\"@reconstructed_quorum_commits_change\\\",\n   \\\"kind\\\": \\\"fact\\\",\n   \\\"statement\\\": \\\"Because the appended configuration entry is immediately the leader's latest configuration and the leader's commitment is rebuilt from it, the quorum that commits a membership change is the reconstructed one, not the committed configuration's quorum: with a reconstruction that has fewer voters than the committed configuration, a change can be committed with support that is not a majority of the configuration being replaced and can include a peer that is not in it, and the peers of the committed configuration that the reconstruction no longer counts as voters are not asked for support at all.\\\",\n   \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"A node whose reconstruction is smaller than the committed configuration leads; a client membership change is issued to that leader with prevIndex 0; the reconstruction keeps the other peers as members so replication can still reach them. This is source reasoning: no execution in this run issued a client membership change to a node with a reconstructed configuration, so the size of the rewritten membership and the endpoints' response are unobserved.\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"change_gate\\\",\\\"append_config_change\\\",\\\"next_configuration\\\",\\\"commitment_set_config\\\",\\\"scan_start\\\",\\\"restore_lastapplied\\\"]}\n ],\n \\\"gaps\\\": [\n  {\\\"investigation_id\\\": \\\"2708fe4120de4b7b945ec449b641cfed-question-0\\\",\n   \\\"question\\\": \\\"Does a client membership change issued to a node whose configuration is the reconstructed one produce a committed configuration that the previous committed configuration's majority never agreed to, and what do the peers it demotes or removes observe and adopt?\\\"}\n ],\n \\\"investigations\\\": [\n  {\\\"id\\\": \\\"2708fe4120de4b7b945ec449b641cfed-question-0\\\",\n   \\\"discriminator\\\": \\\"Whether a client membership change (AddVoter, DemoteVoter or RemoveServer with prevIndex 0) issued to a reconstruction-governed leader rewrites the committed configuration with support that is not a majority of the configuration it replaces, and whether the demoted or removed peers adopt that change; the exercised consequences recorded in the current account remain settled, and this is the one channel left untested.\\\"}\n ],\n \\\"interpretations\\\": [\n  {\\\"investigation_id\\\": \\\"2708fe4120de4b7b945ec449b641cfed-question-0\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"scan_start\\\",\\\"restore_lastapplied\\\",\\\"cfg_entry\\\",\\\"change_gate\\\",\\\"append_config_change\\\",\\\"next_configuration\\\",\\\"commitment_set_config\\\",\\\"leader_commitment\\\",\\\"follower_gate\\\",\\\"existing_test\\\"],\n   \\\"conclusion\\\": \\\"unresolved\\\",\n   \\\"defect_claim\\\": \\\"unresolved\\\",\n   \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Question-level supplement to the current account, which still stands on its receipts for everything exercised: the reconstruction diverges in both directions and across five shapes, and it produces bounded non-progress, leadership and commits resting on a minority, a client-acknowledged commit either resting on one copy or discarded, a vote granted and durably recorded for a peer without a vote, and leadership acquired by a peer without a vote. The account's one untested channel is now explicit: a leader computes membership changes from configurations.latest and rebuilds its commitment from the new configuration, so on a node whose latest configuration is the reconstruction a client change with prevIndex 0 is computed against the wrong membership and committed under the reconstructed quorum, which can demote or remove peers of the committed configuration that were never asked for support and admit a peer that the configuration being replaced does not contain [change_gate, append_config_change, next_configuration, commitment_set_config]. Nothing in the exercised receipts shows a client issuing such a change, so the size of the rewritten membership and the peers' adoption of it are unobserved; the source reasoning is recorded as behaviour and as a necessary gap rather than as an executed consequence, and the defect judgment for this channel stays unresolved until it is executed.\\\",\n   \\\"counterevidence\\\": [\n    \\\"The gate requires the leader's own latest configuration to be committed and a committed entry in its term, so the change is not accepted before the reconstruction is internally stable: the defect is the content of the configuration consulted, not a missing stability check.\\\",\n    \\\"A caller that passes the committed configuration's index as prevIndex is rejected with \\\\\\\"configuration changed since\\\\\\\" rather than served, so the channel requires prevIndex 0, which the package's own AddPeer and RemovePeer helpers use.\\\"],\n   \\\"limitations\\\": [\n    \\\"Source reasoning only: no execution in this run issued a client membership change to a node with a reconstructed configuration.\\\",\n    \\\"The size of the rewritten membership, the peers' adoption of it and any concurrent leadership among the disjoint configurations are unobserved and deliberately not claimed.\\\"]}\n ]\n}\nopen('update.json','w').write(json.dumps(sub, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\nprint('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_12-31-30-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -4\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
