ount's one untested channel is now explicit: a leader computes membership changes from configurations.latest and rebuilds its commitment from the new configuration, so on a node whose latest configuration is the reconstruction a client change with prevIndex 0 is computed against the wrong membership and committed under the reconstructed quorum, which can demote or remove peers of the committed configuration that were never asked for support and admit a peer that the configuration being replaced does not contain [change_gate, append_config_change, next_configuration, commitment_set_config]. Nothing in the exercised receipts shows a client issuing such a change, so the size of the rewritten membership and the peers' adoption of it are unobserved; the source reasoning is recorded as behaviour and as a necessary gap rather than as an executed consequence, and the defect judgment for this channel stays unresolved until it is executed.\\\",\n   \\\"counterevidence\\\": [\n    \\\"The gate requires the leader's own latest configuration to be committed and a committed entry in its term, so the change is not accepted before the reconstruction is internally stable: the defect is the content of the configuration consulted, not a missing stability check.\\\",\n    \\\"A caller that passes the committed configuration's index as prevIndex is rejected with \\\\\\\"configuration changed since\\\\\\\" rather than served, so the channel requires prevIndex 0, which the package's own AddPeer and RemovePeer helpers use.\\\"],\n   \\\"limitations\\\": [\n    \\\"Source reasoning only: no execution in this run issued a client membership change to a node with a reconstructed configuration.\\\",\n    \\\"The size of the rewritten membership, the peers' adoption of it and any concurrent leadership among the disjoint configurations are unobserved and deliberately not claimed.\\\"]}\n ]\n}\nopen('update.json','w').write(json.dumps(sub, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\nprint('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_12-31-30-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -4\"","aggregated_output":"written\n{\"valid\": true, \"run_id\": \"d8459ce0e23540cea18c9bc82878e37d\", \"elapsed_seconds\": 2765.970319849999, \"diagnostics\": [], \"meaning\": \"Read-only validation of these bytes and saved state; no acceptance, execution or budget reservation\", \"no_change\": false, \"execution_requested\": false, \"effects\": [{\"object\": \"sources\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"change_gate\"}, {\"object\": \"sources\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"append_config_change\"}, {\"object\": \"sources\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"next_configuration\"}, {\"object\": \"sources\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"commitment_set_config\"}, {\"object\": \"knowledge\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"@client_change_on_reconstructed_leader\"}, {\"object\": \"knowledge\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"@reconstructed_quorum_commits_change\"}, {\"object\": \"investigations\", \"action\": \"update\", \"target\": \"2708fe4120de4b7b945ec449b641cfed-question-0\", \"changed_fields\": [\"discriminator\", \"gaps\"]}, {\"object\": \"interpretations\", \"action\": \"append\", \"target\": \"interpretations[0]\", \"investigation_id\": \"2708fe4120de4b7b945ec449b641cfed-question-0\", \"changed_fields\": [\"experiment_id\", \"source_ids\", \"executions\", \"conclusion\", \"defect_claim\", \"rationale\", \"counterevidence\", \"limitations\"]}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Made the one untested consequence channel explicit without claiming it. Two source-grounded entries were added: a leader accepts a client membership change as soon as its own latest configuration is committed and it has committed an entry in its term, then computes the new configuration from configurations.latest, installs it immediately and rebuilds its commitment from it (the request's prevIndex being the only guard, with the package's own AddPeer and RemovePeer helpers passing 0); and, because of that, the quorum committing such a change is the reconstructed one rather than the committed configuration's quorum, so with a smaller reconstruction the change can be committed with support that is not a majority of the configuration being replaced, can include a peer that configuration does not contain, and never asks the peers the reconstruction no longer counts. I registered the matching necessary gap (does a client change issued to a reconstruction-governed leader produce a committed configuration the previous majority never agreed to, and what do the demoted peers observe and adopt?), updated the question's discriminator to that channel, and appended a question-level supplement with conclusion and defect judgment unresolved that explicitly keeps the exercised account intact under its receipts. No execution was spent; the channel is source-reasoned only, and the peers' adoption and any concurrent leadership among disjoint configurations are deliberately left unclaimed.\"}"}}
